  "final_span": "honest or not. The answers were mixed. Forty-three percent of Republicans stated that their chosen candidate was trustworthy. According to the poll, half of those identifying as Hispanic and one-quarter of Anglos thought Cruz was honest, while nearly one-quarter of Hispanics regarded O\u2019Rourke as honest. Ipsos used a convenience sample of 1,005 self-identified \u201cadministered in English and Spanish\u201d in Texas, according to the poll. Between Sept. 11 and 12, the poll was carried out. The modest sample size is common in Ipsos online polls, as Jackson noted. But that\u2019s not to say \u201cthere won\u2019t be any error.\u201d The margin of error \u201ccould be plus or minus than margin of error,\u201d he said. While most online polls have larger-than-threshold margins of error, Ipsos\u2019 polls don\u2019t since 2017",
